        <h1 class="post-detail__title">Executive Director Plans to Leave the Valley</h1>

        <div class="post-detail__featured-image">
          <img src="/assets/images/news/50613.webp" alt="Executive Director Plans to Leave the Valley" loading="lazy">
        </div>

        <div class="post-detail__content">
          <p>Tim Adams, Executive Director of the Community Foundation of Teton Valley, announced that he will be stepping down and moving to warmer climes in Boise at the end of November. The Community Foundation of Teton Valley is grateful for Tim’s four years of unwavering leadership across the nonprofit community and for keeping nonprofits’ well-being at the heart of every decision, program, and workshop proposed.</p>

<p><em>“Both staff and Board are saddened by Tim’s resignation but so appreciative of his incredible guidance over the past four years. He has enhanced and grown the Community Foundation’s reach, from Competitive Grants to Tin Cup,</em>” said Astrid Warden, the Foundation’s Board Chair.</p>

<p>Board and staff will work alongside Tim through November, assuring that the Community Foundation of Teton Valley will continue to be the hub for local nonprofits – providing resources, workshops, competitive grants, and our cornerstone fundraising program, the Tin Cup Challenge. The Foundation’s Board is convening a Search Committee and will post the position in the coming weeks. In the meantime, the Community Foundation is excited to celebrate our nonprofit partners through the generosity of Tin Cup Business &amp; Community Challengers during the upcoming 15<sup>th</sup> Annual Tin Cup Challenge Awards Celebration on August 24<sup>th</sup> at the Moose Creek Ranch!</p>

</figure>
